{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-leaks fixture",
    "description": "The `process-evap-leaks` fixture: 128 rows of MOVESOutput computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. Ports docs/evap-leaks.md end to end -- the activity chain A1-A10, the cohort structure C1-C4, the evaporative operating-mode distribution E1-E3, the calculator L1/L8/L9 and the output row O1-O3 -- and it is the only document in this repository whose numbers come off disk.\n\nWHAT IS COMPUTED AND WHAT IS DECLARED, because that is the whole question a fixture has to answer honestly.\n\nCOMPUTED, from the input tables and nothing else: every number. The activity, the cohort fractions, the fuel-usage rebase, the operating-mode distribution including the zero that makes this slice independent of finding F12, the weighted base rates, the emission and the SCC. Nothing is read from the reference -- `sho`, `sourcehours`, `sourcebindistributionfuelusage_13_26161_2020`, `opmodedistributiontemp`, `fractionofoperating` and `MOVESOutput` are all generator output or expected output, and none of them is consumed here. `evl_movesoutput` is declared, as its NONROAD counterpart is, so that the other half of the comparison is version-controlled beside the inputs; it is consumed by nothing.\n\nCOMPUTED, and worth saying so because a reader would assume otherwise: the SHAPES. The activity relation's 82 rows are `n_agecategory x n_runspecday` and the cohort relation's 164 are `n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype`, both metaparameter expressions over extents the runtime discovers from the files (esm-spec 9.7.6). A fixture that wrote 82 or 164 would be asserting the snapshot's shape rather than measuring it (docs/esm-conventions.md 11).\n\nDECLARED: one number, `n_outputCohort` = 64, and the block structure of the output relation. The 128 output rows are 64 surviving (fuelTypeID, modelYearID) cohorts x 2 day types, and WHICH 64 survive is a result of the chain, not an input to it -- so materialising them as an index set is `skolem` / `distinct` / `rank` value invention, which validates and materialises EMPTY (finding F5), and the `ragged` kind advertised for a ragged key set ignores its own member factor (F14). `fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm` declares `output_rows: 12` for the same reason. Three things keep the declaration honest, and the third is the one that matters: (a) the key COLUMNS are not transcribed -- `out_cohortOrdinal` is arithmetic on the aggregate's own loop symbol and `out_fuelTypeID` / `out_modelYearID` come from a join to the cohort relation, exactly as nr-logging-county's `out_ageOrdinal` does; (b) `n_agecategory` carries the gasoline block length, so 41 of the 64 is discovered; (c) the document COMPUTES the surviving-cohort count from the chain and asserts it equals 64, so a chain that produced 63 fails here, before the comparator sees a row. docs/evap-leaks.md 7.2 measured that `require_exact_key_set` catches none of this chain's six ablations and the per-cell gate catches all of them, so the declaration forfeits nothing that was measuring anything -- but it is a declaration and it is named as one.\n\nNO ELEMENT TYPE IS DECLARED, deliberately. docs/esm-conventions.md 18.4 has the reason: MOVES stores these working tables in FLOAT and evaluates in MariaDB's DOUBLE, so the reference for this chain IS binary64 arithmetic, and the sub-1e-7 storage drift between steps is smaller than the six-significant-figure column storage docs/evap-leaks.md 7.1 attributes every residual to. There is no Fortran and no associativity contract to reproduce. If a future document declares Float32 it needs a per-variable Float64 override on `era_sourceBinID`, which is 6.0e10 times binary32's 2^24 limit where an SCC is 135 times it.\n\nF15: the checked-in document carries a `${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}` placeholder it cannot itself ingest, because a `url_template` is neither environment-expanded nor resolved relative to the referencing file. `run-tests.sh` materialises a resolved copy under `.fixtures-run/` and first checks that this document still CANNOT ingest, so the substitution cannot become dead weight unnoticed.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "evaporative", "fixture", "process-evap-leaks"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
    "evl_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["scope"], "note": "1 row. The run's analysis year. docs/evap-leaks.md 0.1: the scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    },
    "evl_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
