    "n_emissionratebyage": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in emissionratebyage." },
    "n_agecategory": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in agecategory. The FIRST factor of both derived axes: 41 model years for the cohort relation and 41 ages for the activity relation, discovered rather than written." },
    "n_soakactivityfraction": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in soakactivityfraction." },
    "n_opmodepolprocassoc": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in opmodepolprocassoc." },
    "n_pollutantprocessassoc": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in pollutantprocessassoc." },
    "n_fueltype": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in fueltype." },
    "n_imcoverage": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in imcoverage. ZERO here, and that is the one place the default is also the answer: the table is empty, so L1 produces no cell and L9's blend is the identity. The document still consumes it, so a county with an evap I/M program needs no new column." },
    "n_hourday": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in hourday." },
    "n_dayofanyweek": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in dayofanyweek." },
    "n_link": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in link." },
    "n_outputCohort": { "type": "integer", "default": 64, "description": "THE ONE DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many (fuelTypeID, modelYearID) cohorts reach MOVESOutput. 64 = 41 gasoline model years, 1980-2020, which is n_agecategory of them, plus 23 E85, 1998-2020. Which cohorts survive is a RESULT of the chain -- C2's `stmyFraction > 0` and the absence of any emissionratebyage row for a diesel or electricity bin -- and materialising them as an index set is finding F5's value invention, which validates and materialises empty. So it is declared, as fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm declares `output_rows: 12`, and `cohortSurvivorCount` below computes the same number from the chain so that a test pins the two together." }
  },

